     "S18"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 096988dd, shifting the lead car 1.5 s later at 0.5x failed every run, with the policy at fault. Each failure was a turn into another car, not a rear-end: the route command was RIGHT, yet the planned path curved left, and the ego drifted out of its lane into a pickup (vehicle 41) in the left lane. A milder setting on the same scene (1 s later, 0.75x) passed.",
    "settings": [
     "S6",
     "S5"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "Settings on 023b7fcc, 09a95ffa, 0e899dd3 and 19f339ba that were repeated several times passed every run. This includes slowing the lead car (0.75x at -0.5 s, 0.5x at -0.5 s) and speeding it up (1.25x to 1.5x with the lead car moved earlier). Their ranges still allow failure rates up to the 0.4 level, so they are not shown to be safe.",
    "settings": [
